{"id":"mahabharata-4-039","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":39,"title":"एकोनचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 39 · Arjuna reveals himself","summary":{"en":"Uttara asks where the Pandavas are, and Arjuna reveals that he is Arjuna and that Kanka, Ballava, Tantipala, Granthika and the sairandhri are his brothers and Draupadi. He recites his ten names and their meanings to convince the prince, and Uttara, his fear gone, bows to him.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರೆಲ್ಲಿ ಎಂದು ಉತ್ತರನು ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ, ತಾನೇ ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಕಂಕ, ಬಲ್ಲವ, ತಂತಿಪಾಲ, ಗ್ರಂಥಿಕ ತನ್ನ ಸಹೋದರರು, ಸೈರಂಧ್ರಿ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಎಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಜಕುಮಾರನಿಗೆ ನಂಬಿಕೆ ಬರಲು ತನ್ನ ಹತ್ತು ಹೆಸರುಗಳನ್ನೂ ಅವುಗಳ ಅರ್ಥಗಳನ್ನೂ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭಯ ಹೋದ ಉತ್ತರನು ನಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"उत्तर पूछता है कि पाण्डव कहाँ हैं, और अर्जुन बताते हैं कि वे स्वयं अर्जुन हैं और कङ्क, बल्लव, तन्तिपाल, ग्रन्थिक उनके भाई तथा सैरन्ध्री द्रौपदी हैं। राजकुमार को विश्वास दिलाने के लिए वे अपने दस नाम और उनके अर्थ बताते हैं, और भयमुक्त उत्तर उन्हें प्रणाम करता है।","te":"పాండవులు ఎక్కడ అని ఉత్తరుడు అడగగా, తానే అర్జునుడనని, కంకుడు, బల్లవుడు, తంతిపాలుడు, గ్రంథికుడు తన సోదరులని, సైరంధ్రి ద్రౌపది అని అర్జునుడు వెల్లడిస్తాడు. రాజకుమారునికి నమ్మకం కలిగించడానికి తన పది పేర్లు, వాటి అర్థాలు చెబుతాడు; భయం తొలగిన ఉత్తరుడు నమస్కరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் எங்கே என்று உத்தரன் கேட்க, தானே அர்ஜுனன், கங்கன், வல்லவன், தந்திபாலன், க்ரந்திகன் தன் சகோதரர்கள், ஸைரந்த்ரி திரௌபதி என்று அர்ஜுனன் வெளிப்படுத்துகிறான். இளவரசனுக்கு நம்பிக்கை வர, தன் பத்துப் பெயர்களையும் அவற்றின் பொருளையும் சொல்ல, அச்சம் நீங்கிய உத்தரன் அவனை வணங்குகிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ എവിടെയെന്ന് ഉത്തരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. താൻ അർജുനനാണെന്നും, കങ്കൻ, ബല്ലവൻ, തന്തിപാലൻ, ഗ്രന്ഥികൻ, സൈരന്ധ്രി എന്നിവർ സഹോദരന്മാരും ദ്രൗപദി സഹോദരിയുമാണെന്നും അർജുനൻ വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു. രാജകുമാരനെ ബോധ്യപ്പെടുത്താൻ തന്റെ പത്തു പേരുകളും അവയുടെ അർഥവും അദ്ദേഹം ചൊല്ലുന്നു. ഭയം മാറിയ ഉത്തരൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വണങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.39; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सुवर्णविकृतानीमान्यायुधानि महात्मनाम् ।\nरुचिराणि प्रकाशन्ते पार्थानामाशुकारिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These gold-adorned weapons of the great-souled, swift Pandavas shine beautifully."}},{"n":2,"text":"क्व नु स्विदर्जुनः पार्थः कौरव्यो वा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where then are Arjuna son of Pritha, King Yudhishthira the Kuru, Nakula, Sahadeva and Bhimasena the Pandava?"}},{"n":3,"text":"सर्व एव महात्मानः सर्वामित्रविनाशनाः ।\nराज्यमक्षैः पराकीर्य न श्रूयन्ते कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these great-souled destroyers of all their enemies have lost their kingdom at dice, and have never been heard of since."}},{"n":4,"text":"द्रौपदी क्व च पाञ्चाली स्त्रीरत्नमिति विश्रुता ।\nजितानक्षैस्तदा कृष्णा तानेवान्वगमद्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And where is Draupadi of Panchala, famed as a jewel among women? When they lost at dice, Krishna followed them into the forest."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अहमस्म्यर्जुनः पार्थः सभास्तारो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nबल्लवो भीमसेनस्तु पितुस्ते रसपाचकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am Arjuna son of Pritha; Yudhishthira is the court attendant at the assembly, Bhimasena is Ballava, your father's cook,"}},{"n":6,"text":"अश्वबन्धोऽथ नकुलः सहदेवस्तु गोकुले ।\nसैरन्ध्रीं द्रौपदीं विद्धि यत्कृते कीचका हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula is the keeper of the horses, Sahadeva is in the cattle camp, and know Sairandhri to be Draupadi, for whose sake the Kichakas were killed.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"दश पार्थस्य नामानि यानि पूर्वं श्रुतानि मे ।\nप्रब्रूयास्तानि यदि मे श्रद्दध्यां सर्वमेव ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you can tell me the ten names of Partha that I heard before, I will believe all you say.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"हन्त तेऽहं समाचक्षे दश नामानि यानि मे ।\nअर्जुनः फल्गुनो जिष्णुः किरीटी श्वेतवाहनः ।\nबीभत्सुर्विजयः कृष्णः सव्यसाची धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Very well, I will tell you my ten names: Arjuna, Phalguna, Jishnu, Kiritin, Shvetavahana, Bibhatsu, Vijaya, Krishna, Savyasachin and Dhananjaya.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"केनासि विजयो नाम केनासि श्वेतवाहनः ।\nकिरीटी नाम केनासि सव्यसाची कथं भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why are you called Vijaya, why Shvetavahana, why Kiritin, and how are you Savyasachin?"}},{"n":10,"text":"अर्जुनः फल्गुनो जिष्णुः कृष्णो बीभत्सुरेव च ।\nधनंजयश्च केनासि प्रब्रूहि मम तत्त्वतः ।\nश्रुता मे तस्य वीरस्य केवला नामहेतवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And why Arjuna, Phalguna, Jishnu, Krishna, Bibhatsu and Dhananjaya? Tell me truly; I have heard only the bare names of that hero, not their reasons.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"सर्वाञ्जनपदाञ्जित्वा वित्तमाच्छिद्य केवलम् ।\nमध्ये धनस्य तिष्ठामि तेनाहुर्मां धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because I conquered all the countries and took all their wealth, and I stand in the midst of riches, they call me Dhananjaya."}},{"n":12,"text":"अभिप्रयामि संग्रामे यदहं युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nनाजित्वा विनिवर्तामि तेन मां विजयं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because I go into battle against warriors wild for fighting and never turn back without defeating them, they know me as Vijaya."}},{"n":13,"text":"श्वेताः काञ्चनसंनाहा रथे युज्यन्ति मे हयाः ।\nसंग्रामे युध्यमानस्य तेनाहं श्वेतवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because white horses with golden harness are yoked to my chariot when I fight in battle, I am Shvetavahana."}},{"n":14,"text":"उत्तराभ्यां च पूर्वाभ्यां फल्गुनीभ्यामहं दिवा ।\nजातो हिमवतः पृष्ठे तेन मां फल्गुनं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because I was born by day on the slope of the Himalaya under the two Phalgunis, Uttara and Purva, they call me Phalguna."}},{"n":15,"text":"पुरा शक्रेण मे दत्तं युध्यतो दानवर्षभैः ।\nकिरीटं मूर्ध्नि सूर्याभं तेन माहुः किरीटिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because long ago Shakra gave me a sun-bright crown for my head when I fought the chief of the Danavas, they call me Kiritin."}},{"n":16,"text":"न कुर्यां कर्म बीभत्सं युध्यमानः कथंचन ।\nतेन देवमनुष्येषु बीभत्सुरिति मां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because I never commit a hideous deed in battle, among gods and men they know me as Bibhatsu."}},{"n":17,"text":"उभौ मे दक्षिणौ पाणी गाण्डीवस्य विकर्षणे ।\nतेन देवमनुष्येषु सव्यसाचीति मां विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because both my hands are skilled in drawing the Gandiva, among gods and men they call me Savyasachin."}},{"n":18,"text":"पृथिव्यां चतुरन्तायां वर्णो मे दुर्लभः समः ।\nकरोमि कर्म शुक्लं च तेन मामर्जुनं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because my pure color is rare on the earth bounded by four seas, and I do bright deeds, they know me as Arjuna."}},{"n":19,"text":"अहं दुरापो दुर्धर्षो दमनः पाकशासनिः ।\nतेन देवमनुष्येषु जिष्णुनामास्मि विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because I am hard to reach and hard to overcome, a subduer, the son of Indra, I am famed among gods and men as Jishnu."}},{"n":20,"text":"कृष्ण इत्येव दशमं नाम चक्रे पिता मम ।\nकृष्णावदातस्य सतः प्रियत्वाद्बालकस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father gave me Krishna as the tenth name, out of love for the dark, radiant child.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः पार्थं स वैराटिरभ्यवादयदन्तिकात् ।\nअहं भूमिंजयो नाम नाम्नाहमपि चोत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata's son bowed to Partha close by: \"I am Bhumimjaya, and my name is also Uttara."}},{"n":22,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्वां पार्थ पश्यामि स्वागतं ते धनंजय ।\nलोहिताक्ष महाबाहो नागराजकरोपम ।\nयदज्ञानादवोचं त्वां क्षन्तुमर्हसि तन्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune I see you, Partha. Welcome, Dhananjaya, red-eyed, mighty-armed one, with arms like elephant trunks. Forgive me for what I said to you through ignorance."}},{"n":23,"text":"यतस्त्वया कृतं पूर्वं विचित्रं कर्म दुष्करम् ।\nअतो भयं व्यतीतं मे प्रीतिश्च परमा त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of the wonderful, hard deeds you did before, my fear has gone, and I have the greatest love for you.\""}}]}]}